# R Architecture Rules

## Directory Structure
```
R/
  data_processing.R     # data ingestion + cleaning functions
  features.R            # feature engineering functions
  modeling.R            # model fitting + evaluation functions
  visualization.R       # ggplot2 plot functions
  utils.R               # shared utilities (type checks, formatters)
analysis/
  01_eda.qmd            # exploratory data analysis
  02_modeling.qmd       # model training + evaluation
  03_report.qmd         # stakeholder-facing output
tests/
  testthat/
    test_data_processing.R
    test_features.R
    test_modeling.R
data/
  raw/                  # never modified, gitignored if large
  processed/            # cleaned data, committed if small
  fixtures/             # test fixtures, always committed
plumber/
  api.R                 # Plumber API (if exposing predictions)
renv.lock               # committed
_quarto.yml             # project-level Quarto config
```

## Function Signatures
- Input: tidyverse-style (first arg is data frame, returns data frame for pipeline-ability)
- Output: explicit return type documented in roxygen2 `@return`
- No global state: functions read from arguments only, never from `Sys.getenv()` inside — pass config as argument

## Tidy Evaluation Pattern
For functions that take column names as arguments:
```r
compute_ratio <- function(df, numerator, denominator) {
  df |>
    dplyr::mutate(ratio = {{ numerator }} / {{ denominator }})
}
```
Never use `deparse(substitute())` or `eval(parse(...))`.

## Plumber API Pattern
Plumber endpoints are thin wrappers around `R/` functions:
```r
#* @post /predict
#* @param features JSON features object
function(features) {
  df <- jsonlite::fromJSON(features)
  result <- predict_model(df)  # from R/modeling.R
  list(prediction = result)
}
```
